<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell 18 points to 1,314.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell 18 points to 1,314.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for</p>
<p>spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,314 today from</p>
<p>1,332 on April 21, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals</p>
<p>1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates</p>
<p>in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1325    12.025	  1345    12.206</p>
<p>   1a   1342 10163.000	  1356 10269.000</p>
<p>   2    1555    22.219	  1575    22.500</p>
<p>   2a   1540 12631.000	  1575 12913.000</p>
<p>   3    1440    13.281	  1467    13.531</p>
